all the tool, emit the tool call itself.\nIf you use MOUSE, include integer row and col arguments.\nEFFICIENCY BUDGET \u2014 your score on each level is (baseline_actions / your_actions)^2, so every wasted action costs you quadratically.\nLevel 1: you have used 50 actions; a strong score needs about 39 or fewer. You are 1.3x over the target.\nIf you are not steadily making progress toward the level goal, commit to your single best hypothesis and the shortest sequence that tests it \u2014 do not exhaustively scan rows/columns or enumerate every option. Test one idea, read the result, then decide.", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\n\ndef node_by_color(frame, col):\n    for n in frame.segmentation['nodes']:\n        if n['color']==col:\n            return n\n    return None\nb = node_by_color(current_frame,'b')\nprint('blue boundary', b['boundary'])\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL RESULT: python", "content": "blue boundary [[12, 16], [12, 35], [15, 35], [15, 16]]", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\n\n# UP moved blue back up 4 rows. So vertical movement works.\n# The goal likely is to place blue onto the yellow U's. Yellow U's are at rows52-59. Blue is at rows12-15. Need ~10 DOWN moves (4 rows per move = 40 rows). From 12 to 52 is 40 rows, so 10 DOWNs.\n# But blue is 20 cols wide, yellow U's are maybe 12 cols wide each. Need to align horizontally.\n# Let's try to move blue horizontally to align over left yellow U. Left yellow U is at cols 16-27? From segmentation boundary: [[52,16],[52,19],[55,19],[56,20],[56,23],[55,24],[52,24],[52,27],[59,27],[59,16]]. So leftmost col 16, rightmost 27. Blue cols 16-35 currently. Overlap 16-27. Maybe need exact alignment where blue sits on top of U opening? Could be need to align center